@3.1 Loops
.
=3.1 LOOPS
.
=SYNTAX
.
:GP.DO [count]
:    ...
:GP.LOOP
.
=WHAT IT COSTS
.
.  ASM: GP.DO GP.LOOP GP.EXITDO
.    ASM -- a keyword, run by machine code in the GP runtime block. A program
.    using ANY GP keyword pays for the whole block.
.
=DESCRIPTION
.
.Counted loop, modelled on prog8's repeat. Count 0 or omitted loops forever.
.Nesting works.
.
:GP.EXITDO
.
.Leave the innermost GP.DO early, closing its stack frame on the way. This is
.the leak-free exit -- a GOTO out of a GP.DO abandons the frame, and the
.frames do not get reclaimed.
.
:GP.DO
:  TICK = TICK + 1
:  IF TICK = 9 THEN GP.EXITDO
:GP.LOOP
.
=EXAMPLE PROGRAM
.
.  LOOPS.EXP.BL -- runnable, in the GPC-BASIC folder
